## 7. Mounting ConfigMaps as Volumes

ConfigMaps can also be mounted as files inside containers.

Example:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: config-volume-demo
spec:
  containers:
    - name: nginx
      image: nginx
      volumeMounts:
        - name: config-volume
          mountPath: /etc/config
  volumes:
    - name: config-volume
      configMap:
        name: app-config
```

Apply:

```bash
kubectl apply -f config-volume.yaml
```

Check mounted files:

```bash
kubectl exec config-volume-demo -- ls /etc/config
```

Read a configuration file:

```bash
kubectl exec config-volume-demo -- cat /etc/config/DB_HOST
```

---

## 8. Mounting Secrets as Volumes

Secrets can also be mounted as files inside containers.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: secret-volume-demo
spec:
  containers:
    - name: nginx
      image: nginx
      volumeMounts:
        - name: secret-volume
          mountPath: /etc/secret
          readOnly: true
  volumes:
    - name: secret-volume
      secret:
        secretName: db-secret
```

Apply:

```bash
kubectl apply -f secret-volume.yaml
```

The Secret data becomes available as files inside `/etc/secret`.

